Projection in spring data jpa
###############################
n Spring Data JPA, projection is a way to fetch only specific fields from an entity instead of retrieving the entire object. This is useful when:

You don’t need all the columns of a table.

You want to improve performance by reducing data transfer.

You want to expose only certain fields in APIs.

Types of Projections
Interface-based projection  
Define an interface with getters for the fields you want.

Class-based (DTO) projection  
Use a constructor expression to map query results into a DTO.

Dynamic projection  
Let the repository method decide which projection to use at runtime.

